# Why this file exists: several tests read a source file as text and match it
# with regexes anchored on `$` or `\n`. In a JavaScript regex `.` does not match
# `\r`, so on a CRLF checkout `/^COPY\s+(.+)$/` matches nothing and the test
# fails against source that is perfectly fine. Six test files broke that way on
# Windows (33 assertions), and `prettier --check` flagged all 75 files it looks
# at, because its endOfLine default is "lf". CI runs on Linux and saw none of it.
#
# The blobs in this repository are already LF — core.autocrlf=true converts on
# checkout, not on commit — so this pins the working tree to what git already
# stores. It changes no file content.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# The two that genuinely want CRLF. cmd.exe mis-parses a multi-line label or
# goto in an LF batch file, and START.bat is how this app is launched.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Never touched, never diffed.
*.png           binary
*.ico           binary

# Vendored third-party bundles are kept byte-for-byte as upstream shipped them.
# chart.min.js was committed with CRLF; renormalising it would rewrite 40 lines
# of minified code we do not maintain, for no benefit.
lib/**          -text
